[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470462049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470462049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470462049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQEJh","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T12:56:14Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T12:56:14Z","body":"Notice how a [previous job](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/11797684482/job/32862209988?pr=99124) failed because of multi-commits, but the latest succeeds because i squashed my commits.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470462049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470465308","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470465308","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470465308,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQE8c","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T12:57:48Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T12:57:48Z","body":"I don't think this is an appropriate approach for multiple reasons, main one is that multiple commits are fine until the PR should be merged, and are actively encouraged when appropriate, where reviewing things in parts is necessary\r\n\r\nThat's why we normally request squashing only after all other review is done\r\n\r\nSecond there *are* valid multi-commit PRs, like ones introducing git-blame-ignore etc.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470465308/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470480533","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470480533","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470480533,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQIqV","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:04:58Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:09:59Z","body":"> I don't think this is an appropriate approach for multiple reasons, main one is that multiple commits are fine until the PR should be merged, and are actively encouraged when appropriate, where reviewing things in parts is necessary\r\n\r\nYep, makes sense to me.\r\n\r\nA modification could be to introduce a label like `single-commit` that activates a \"single commit PR\" workflow ([like so](https://stackoverflow.com/a/74829754/730797)).\r\n\r\nMaintainers could pick and choose whether the check should be run by slapping the label on it (or removing it again later).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470480533/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470492743","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470492743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470492743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQLpH","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:10:31Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:16:33Z","body":"I don't think this is needed, asking or helping with squashing is part of the general workflow\r\n\r\nAsking for, or having CI complain about squashed commits, adds additional frustration and work to PRs\r\n\r\nJust like we don't do style and similar review before the relevant teams have gotten a look at a PR to avoid unnecessary work we don't want to add this, again why we don't ask for squashed commits right at the start\r\n\r\nAdding a tag, that needs to be tracked and managed, with fragile CI stuff, feels unnecessary instead of just using the workflow that has worked for years\r\n\r\nEdit: In my experience reviewing *a lot* of PRs including ones from new contributors I don't think I've often seen any strong feelings about squashing commits, quite a few are confused by it before they figure it out sure, but that's true for most parts of the PR process. However I feel that this PR would change that, it would create confusion and frustration from the get-go by having an automated check complain instead of a friendly and helpful message after a PR has been approved","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470492743/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470527927","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470527927","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470527927,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQUO3","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:26:42Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:26:42Z","body":"> Edit: In my experience reviewing a lot of PRs including ones from new contributors I don't think I've often seen any strong feelings about squashing commits, quite a few are confused by it before they figure it out sure, but that's true for most parts of the PR process. However I feel that this PR would change that, it would create confusion and frustration from the get-go by having an automated check complain instead of a friendly and helpful message after a PR has been approved\r\n\r\nHrm yeah, this PR comes from my specific perspective on software development, but I can see how it could be intimidating for new users (instead of coming from a comment).\r\n\r\nI still think it may be net positive, but I'm not married to the PR. Feel free to close (or merge) if it becomes clear there is a consensus among the team.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470527927/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470531389","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470531389","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470531389,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQVE9","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:28:21Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:28:21Z","body":"https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-pull-requests/incorporating-changes-from-a-pull-request/about-pull-request-merges#squash-and-merge-your-commits","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470531389/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470532335","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470532335","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470532335,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQVTv","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:28:46Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:29:21Z","body":"I just don't see what this adds, this isn't like style or documentation checks that actually benefit from automation, it's trivial for the production team or other maintainers to look at the PR and judge if it needs a \"please squash\" message\r\n\r\nIt's not so much the process itself that I question but the need for it itself, this feels to me like one of the things that would benefit the least from automation, I simply don't see the point","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470532335/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470545486","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470545486","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470545486,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQYhO","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:34:32Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:34:57Z","body":"> It's not so much the process itself that I question but the need for it itself, this feels to me like one of the things that would benefit the least from automation, I simply don't see the point\r\n\r\nIt has happened 3 or 4 times to me already that I had a PR ready, but I had forgotten to squash it since it's a pretty unusual requirement from a public repo (i've contributed to a few and haven't run across it before). I'm not sure if this is a common experience or unique to me.\r\n\r\nI prefer having a CI tell me so that I can quickly fix it and move on, other than a maintainer asking me a few days later to squash and then forgetting about the PR again for a bit after my squash (which has unfortunately also happened a few times already).\r\n\r\n> https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-pull-requests/incorporating-changes-from-a-pull-request/about-pull-request-merges#squash-and-merge-your-commits\r\n\r\nI proposed this in a GOP recently (linked above) but it was not very well liked :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470545486/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470555744","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470555744","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470555744,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQbBg","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:39:07Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:39:07Z","body":"> I'm not sure if this is a common experience or unique to me.\r\n\r\nI haven't seen many PRs linger for a long time waiting for the OP to squash their commits, and if it takes a while and the OP doesn't respond the production team normally takes care of it if it's urgent.\r\n\r\n> I proposed this in a GOP recently (linked above) but it was not very well liked :)\r\n\r\nIt wasn't so much not liked as not supported by the limited tools of GitHub","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470555744/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470563354","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470563354","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470563354,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQc4a","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:42:30Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:44:37Z","body":"Thanks for the suggestion, but this is not a good idea for our workflow.\r\n\r\nOur policy is not \"1 PR == 1 commit\" ALWAYS. Our policy is that each commit should be self-contained and bring the engine from a working state A to a working state B. So a hotfix / typo fix / style fix should be amended into the original commit - we don't care post-merge that this was hotfixed during development, we only want the now-good commit in our history.\r\n\r\nBut some PRs are more complex and benefit from multiple commits which bring the engine from a working state A to B to C to D etc. This is typically a workflow used by veteran contributors who know well how to author commits in a way that match our development style - hence why it may sound to newcomers that the policy is \"1 PR == 1 commit\", as newcomers usually don't have this Godot specific experience yet.\r\n\r\nAnd this is one killer reason why we can't use Squash and Merge on GitHub, aside from all the valid reasons Clay outlined in your proposal. We need to be able to make the decision at merge time of whether a PR should have a single commit or if its multiple commit add value to our history and are correctly split. The drop-down button for the merge type on GitHub remembers the last state used, so it makes it very easy (and risky) to wrongly \"Squash and Merge\" a PR whose split history is very valuable, or wrongly forget to \"Squash and Merge\" a PR with 50 WIP commits.\r\n\r\nThe other big reason is indeed the workflow we use for merging PRs in the first place with batch merges, done manually on the command line, which can only be properly registered by GitHub if using a merge commit that will be identified as a merge of the original PR, even if not done by pressing the green button. With a locally-squashed rebased history, there's no way for GitHub to match that to an open PR.\r\n\r\nFinally, a nagging CI check during PR development is more developer-adverse IMO than a maintainer gently asking them to perform an action *once* the PR is ready to merge. For first-time contributors in particular, I often do the squash (and a rebase for good measure) on their PR myself so they don't get needlessly burdened by bureaucracy (especially if they don't seem proficient with Git, which can often be seen with people writing bad commit messages, having a mismatched Git author identity, updating their PR branch with merges, etc.).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470563354/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470568571","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470568571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470568571,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQeJ7","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:44:50Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:44:50Z","body":"While I agree with the above, I will note that this *could* have potential in the form of a warning. Those don't prevent an action from passing, but **will** give a notice in the checks. I can't speak for how easily that could be setup with a standard action, but if you wanted to pursue this idea I'd consider that route instead","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470568571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470607995","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2470607995","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2470607995,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQnx7","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T14:00:38Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T14:00:38Z","body":"A warning for PR mergers could be nice, but I'm not sure what form that could take. It _would_ make sense for those of us merging PRs to have something that lets us know when a PR has more than 1 commit (or, if we find heuristics for it, a \"bad\" commit message), so we can make sure it's intended before merging.\r\n\r\nMaybe that's something that can be done as part of automation on the Merge Queue project used by release managers, so we get this flagged for ourselves automatically.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470607995/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471272702","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99124#issuecomment-2471272702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99124","id":2471272702,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TTKD-","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T18:28:14Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T18:28:14Z","body":"@akien-mga This could be an excellent Github Inc. enhancement request for the Merge Queue project used by release managers, so we would be flagged automatically.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471272702/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]